# .gitleaksignore: fingerprints gitleaks must not report again. One line per finding, and a line is a claim that the
# match is not a secret — so it carries a comment saying why, above it (blank lines and '#' are ignored).
#
# Format: <commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>
# Fingerprints come from the finding itself (JSON report "Fingerprint", or code scanning's alert). They survive a line
# shift, since the commit and the rule are in them. See docs/runbook/ci.md.
